---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Holly Way — The Makers Collective | Waiheke Island Art"
  description="Holly Way is a ceramicist with The Makers Collective, working from Waiheke Island, New Zealand."
>
  <section class="wrap artist">
    <h1>Holly Way</h1>
    <p>
      Holly Way makes pots the slow way — by hand, on a kick wheel she
      restored herself, in a shed she built from reclaimed macrocarpa. Her
      work sits somewhere between functional and sculptural: bowls you
      could eat from, vessels that are really just studies in a particular
      curve. She fires almost everything in a wood kiln she and a few other
      island potters maintain together, which means no two pieces ever come
      out quite the same — an unpredictability she's stopped trying to
      control.
    </p>
    <p>
      Holly moved to Waiheke from Nelson eight years ago after an
      apprenticeship with a potter there, and describes her practice now as
      "arguing with the clay until we agree on something." She favours
      unglazed, textural surfaces over the high-gloss finishes more common
      in commercial ceramics, and often leaves visible fingerprints and tool
      marks in the final work rather than smoothing them away.
    </p>
    <p>
      Her pieces are made in small batches, usually eight to twelve at a
      time, and she considers each firing its own body of work rather than
      a restock. When she's not at the wheel, Holly forages clay and
      volcanic ash from around the island to test in future glazes, several
      of which are still years from being ready to use.
    </p>
    <a href="/gallery" class="btn">View available work</a>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .artist { padding: 4rem 0 5rem; max-width: 58ch; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center; }
  .artist h1 { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .artist p { text-align: left; }
  .artist .btn { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
